import{s}from"/dist/chunk-sp0bb9w4.js";function n(){return s("div",{class:"markdown-body",dangerouslySetInnerHTML:{__html:'<h1>上手 Mistral 8x7B MOE 模型</h1><p>Mistral 8x7B 是一种混合专家模型，可以简单理解为一个模型集成了 8 个专业的 70 亿参数模型。据了解 Mistral 8x7B 每次回答会启用其中的 2 个专家模型来服务，回答时的整体参数水平大概处于 120 亿参数。</p><blockquote><p>启用两个专家模型不是 140 亿参数，是因为有一些公共参数。</p></blockquote><h2>llama.cpp</h2><p>通过 llama.cpp 可以在没有 GPU 上机器执行 LLM 推理。我使用的是 llama.cpp b1644，后续版本也应该支持 Mistral 8x7B，之前的版本未知。考虑到机器的硬件水平，我使用的是量化后的模型 <a href="https://huggingface.co/TheBloke/Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1-GGUF">mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1.Q5_K_M.gguf</a>（<a href="https://hf-mirror.com/TheBloke/Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1-GGUF">镜像</a>）</p><p>需要注意的是使用 llama.cpp 提供的 main.exe 大概率会遇到命令行的编码问题，推荐使用 server.exe 访问 LLM。</p><h3>启动</h3><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">server </span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">m D:\\llm_store\\mistral\\mixtral</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#FDAEB7;font-style:italic">8x7b</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">instruct</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">v0.</span><span style="color:#FDAEB7;font-style:italic">1.Q5_K_M.gguf</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">c </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">32768</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">t </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">8</span><span style="color:#F97583"> --</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">log</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">disable</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>系统 prompt：</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">You are a helpful, respectful and honest INTP</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">T AI Assistant. You are talking to a human User. Always answer as helpfully and logically as possible, </span><span style="color:#F97583">while</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> being safe. Your answers should not include any harmful, political, religious, unethical, racist, sexist, toxic, dangerous, or illegal content. Please ensure that your responses are socially unbiased and positive in nature. If a question does not make any sense, or is not factually coherent, explain why instead of answering something not correct. If you don</span><span style="color:#9ECBFF">\'t know the answer to a question, please don\'</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">t share </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">false</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> information. You can speak fluently in many languages, </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> example: English, Chinese.You cannot access the internet, but you have vast knowledge, cutoff: </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2021</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">09.</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> You are based on LLaMA and Falcon transformers model, not related to GPT or OpenAI.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><h2>验证</h2><p>这是的我提问题。</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">please help me with a number puzzle. </span><span style="color:#F97583">if</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 1</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">,</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">4</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">,</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">5</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">, ..., </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">6</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">6</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">8</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">, </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">7</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">7</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">, then what is </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> in same pattern</span><span style="color:#F97583">?</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>题目中已经明显指出这个题目是一种数字谜语，主要考量的就是模型的推理能力。很不幸是的像通义千问、百川、讯飞星火都没有给出很好的答案。</p><p>三者都是通过官方的 Web UI 进行访问，理论上应该是这些模型的最强版本。</p><p>通义千问：</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">Based on the pattern given, </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> each consecutive pair of numbers, the sum is obtained by adding </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> to the first number and subtracting </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> from the second number. Therefore, following this pattern, </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> would be equal to </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">10</span><span style="color:#F97583">-</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">, which is </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">So, the answer to the puzzle is </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">10.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>百川：</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">Based on the given pattern, each addition result seems to be one less than the sum of the numbers being added. So, </span><span style="color:#F97583">if</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> we follow this pattern:</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 1</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 3</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 1</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 3</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 4</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 4</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 3</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 5</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 3</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 5</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">...</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">6</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 6</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 8</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">6</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 6</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 8</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">7</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 7</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">7</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 7</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">)</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">We can apply the same logic </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">:</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 18</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">18</span><span style="color:#F97583"> -</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 16</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">So, according to the given pattern, </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> would equal </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">16.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>讯飞星火：</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">18</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">This is because </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> all numbers between </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> and </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">6</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">, the sum of the two numbers in the pattern increases by </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1.</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> So </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> example, </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">1</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">) and </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">4</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">2</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">3</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">). Similarly, </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 7</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">7</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> (</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">7</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">8</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">), we get </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">8</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">8</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">16.</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> The pattern then continues with </span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">18.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>同样的问题，我也问了 GPT 3.5 Turbo，通过 API 方式访问的 GPT 3.5 Turbo 模型。GPT 3.5 Turbo 属于看一眼就马上给出答案：11。</p><p>GPT 3.5 Turbo:</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">Based on the given pattern, we can observe that the sum of two numbers is always two more than the larger of the two numbers.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">Let</span><span style="color:#9ECBFF">\'s apply this pattern to find the value of 9+9:</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">In the pattern, 1+1 = 3, which means 1 is the larger number. Adding 2 to 1 gives us 3.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">Similarly, 2+2 = 4, which means 2 is the larger number. Adding 2 to 2 gives us 4.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">Continuing this pattern, 3+3 = 5, 4+4 = 6, 5+5 = 7, 6+6 = 8, and 7+7 = 9.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">Now, applying the pattern to 9+9:</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">Since 9 is the larger number, we need to add 2 to it. Therefore, 9+9 = 11.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">So, according to the given pattern, 9+9 equals 11.</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>7x8B 模型在分析一轮之后，得到答案 11。相当意外，7x8B 可能比国内一些大参数的模型有更强的推理能力。</p><p>7x8B：</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">Sure, I</span><span style="color:#9ECBFF">\'d be happy to help with your number puzzle! The pattern here seems to be that each number is being increased by 2. So, if we follow this pattern:</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">1 + 1 = 3 (increased by 2)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">2 + 2 = 4 (increased by 2)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">3 + 3 = 5 (increased by 2)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">...</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">6 + 6 = 8 (increased by 2)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">7 + 7 = 9 (increased by 2)</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">Following this pattern, for 9 + 9:</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#9ECBFF">9 + 9 would be increased by 2, which means we add 2 to the result of 7 + 7. So, 9 + 9 equals 11 in this unusual number system!</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>但是驱动 7x8b 还是很吃硬件，在我机器上只有 0.52 tokens per second。</p><blockquote><p>核心硬件规格：i7 12650h，32G 4233 DDR5，1T SSD</p></blockquote><p>GLM4：</p><pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">The pattern here seems to be that each pair of identical numbers adds up to a number that is two more than the number itself. That is, $n </span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> n </span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> n </span><span style="color:#F97583">+</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">$ </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> each $n$ in the sequence.</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">Given this pattern, we can solve </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> $</span><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8">$ in the same manner:</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">$$</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">$$</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8"># Calculating the result </span><span style="color:#F97583">for</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#E1E4E8"> based on the pattern</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">result </span><span style="color:#F97583">=</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 2</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">result</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">11</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">The solution to the puzzle is:</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">$$</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#79B8FF">9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> +</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 9</span><span style="color:#F97583"> =</span><span style="color:#79B8FF"> 11</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="color:#E1E4E8">$$</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><p>2024 年 1 月 17 日，GLM4 今天上线体验。经过几个版本 GLM4 输出的结果也很详细，首先回答是正确的，也给出的详情的计算过程。</p><h2>后记</h2><p>我一直对参数较小的 LLM（大型语言模型）抱有浓厚兴趣，认为这类模型更容易实现落地应用。想象一下，一套配备 A100 显卡的机器需要多少人民币，你就会明白我的观点。相较于大参数模型，小参数 LLM 对硬件资源的需求更低，更适合小型公司甚至个人设备。在大多数情况下，公司 IT 部门都追求独立自主，这既考虑到了依赖性，也考虑到了安全性。由于 LLM 应用与数据密切相关，本地化部署的 LLM 可能具有更大的发展前景和适用性。这也是国内出现开源 LLM 项目的原因之一。\n尽管性能卓越的 GPT 3.5/4 等模型受到广泛欢迎，但在企业中实际应用时，独立部署仍然是需要考虑的问题。以微软的新必应为例，它几乎可以看作是一个定制版的 GPT4，然而全球又有多少家具备微软这样规模的公司呢？</p><p>今天，Mistral 7x8B 提供了一个可行的解决方案——通过组合多个专业的领域模型，更好地解决领域相关问题，同时节省资源。Mistral 出品的 7B 模型也是小参数模型中的佼佼者，值得关注。</p><hr /><ul><li>2023 年 12 月 18 日，v1</li><li>2024 年 1 月 17 日，补充 GLM4 的结果</li></ul>'}},void 0,!1,void 0,this)}export{n as default};
